--- a/docs/fork-touchpoints.md
+++ b/docs/fork-touchpoints.md
@@ -4255,8 +4255,12 @@ The emitted lights and the standalone library shaders keep their physical illumi
 
 - `pass/numos/numos_ground.slangh` owns the sphere intersection and the pinned ground
   lighting without camera extinction. The composite, rainbow and PSR resolver use this
-  surface for hazed misses. The G-buffer and composite binding indices, resource
-  manager and `rtx_numos.cpp` carry both reflected-ground records to the post-depth air.
+  surface for hazed misses. The ground's key shadow follows the physical hit into the
+  cloud frame and filters distant gaps when seen edge-on from the floor.
+- `pass/numos/numos_psr_sky.slangh` shades the outgoing PSR leg against the existing
+  far-air volumes. `rtx_numos.cpp` binds their sampled views for the G-buffer. Both
+  reflection and transmission use their usual path radiance. The resource manager
+  and composite no longer allocate, clear or read reflected-ground records.
 
 ### Enhanced No Horizon
 
